WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.960
It's done!

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.570
Purin, try sitting on it.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.530
Huh?

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.100
P-Purin?!

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.640
Well, I guess it's okay.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.000
No, no, no, it's not okay!

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:04.010
<b>Step 2
Does "DIY" Mean Doing Stuff With Somebody?</b>

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.990
I'm going now.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.680
All right! Be careful!

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.390
You're safe!

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.390
What do you mean?

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.250
So, I joined the DIY club.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.530
The DIY club?

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.740
It's an abbreviation for...

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.740
Do it—

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.700
Yourself, right?

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:26.860
Why are you acting bashful?

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:31.250
Hearing you call me be my full 
name... It feels new, somehow.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.800
I didn't call your name.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.710
And my name is Miku.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.750
I wish you'd stop calling me Purin!

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.000
The thing is, Purin,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.340
if you're wondering why 
I joined the DIY club...

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.600
I'm thinking of making some 
nice stuff. Like a ben—

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.520
Serufu, an old, moldy, antiquated 
DIY club suits you very well.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.730
It suits me, huh?

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.250
Why are you acting bashful?

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.930
I am the opposite of old and moldy.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.610
Everything I'm studying is cutting edge!

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.950
With these hands, I will further advance 
the Fourth Industrial Revolution...

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.370
and bring about a technological singularity.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.630
Through AI, the future will 
become fully automated.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.370
And humans, forget about manual labor...

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.650
humans won't ever have to do a thing!

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.960
Bye!

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.300
Well, I guess I'll head back home now.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.220
Whoops! No, I won't.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.320
I have to get going too.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.380
A future where I won't 
have to do a thing, huh?

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.650
If I never have to do anything...

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:45.390
what will I do?

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.260
Hey! Good morning!

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.260
Mornin'!

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.950
What did you do yesterday?

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.120
Huh? Yesterday?

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.840
I had curry ramen.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.060
I went to Kanegi Fruits.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.390
I'm jealous!

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.960
Takumin!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.040
Morning!

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.820
G-Good morning, S-Serufu-san!

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.490
Morning! Morning. Morning!

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.330
N-Nothing.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:31.030
Um, Serufu-san, what did you do yesterday?

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.990
Hmm, what did I do?

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:39.260
Takumin, if you never had to do 
anything, what would you do?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.060
I'd read more books... I think.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.760
But since I wouldn't have 
to do anything... Wait.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:54.280
That's sort of a philosophical 
question, kind of like a paradox.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.130
Serufu-san, what would you do?

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.050
Well, that's a tough one.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.500
Maybe do a lot of doodling...

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.320
or maybe play with Pochi 
and the others a lot...

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.960
or maybe take naps...

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:16.240
"My only love sprung from my only hate!"

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:20.550
"Too early seen unknown and known too late!"

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:24.660
"Prodigious birth of love it is to me,"

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.170
turtle (kame)

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.170
(tsuru)   true

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.170
tsuru
(crane)

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.170
(kame) 
turtle

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.170
turtle

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.230
Come true...

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.630
With a Gentle Face
and Kind Words

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.100
What? Takumin, you made that yourself?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.840
That's amazing!

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.070
It's so pretty! And so meticulous!

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.970
Th-Thank you.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.020
Have I told you that I joined the DIY club?

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.080
No, not yet! So, you've decided on a club?

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:45.940
Yeah.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.400
Oh! DIY means "Do it—"

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.420
Yourself, right?

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.860
Yua Serufu!

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.490
Is that why you joined?

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.950
That outcome was just happenstance.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.160
That outcome was just happenstance, was it?

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.940
Purin said that a DIY club was outdated.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.170
Purin?

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.960
She's always getting angry, you see,

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.390
and she puffs out her 
cheeks like a pufferfish.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.600
Purin gets angry like a pufferfish?

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:24.700
They said that if the DIY club doesn't 
get enough members, it'll be disbanded.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:29.230
In novels about clubs, that 
plot point happens a lot.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.420
Does it?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:36.830
<b>Sunflower 
Girls</b>

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:36.820
I love this book.
 It's called <i>Sunflower Girls</i>.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:42.060
They can't find enough members, so their 
gardening club is in danger of being disbanded.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.250
That's exactly the same situation.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:49.070
Then the gardening club hands out flowers 
in order to gather new members.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.080
Flowers?

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.360
Yes! Beautiful, lovely flowers.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:56.050
Because they want people to 
become interested in gardening.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.970
I see.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:03.460
Then maybe we in the DIY club 
should hand out lumber!

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.410
I don't think anyone will want that.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.330
Nails!

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.520
I'm not sure that will 
gain people's interest.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.120
Really? Where?

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.360
They say that over near Work One, a place 
called the Kenshin Cafe just opened.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:19.970
I heard that all the workers 
wear a gyounin hood.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.960
<b>Gyounin Hood</b>

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.600
Really? Let's go on our way home!

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.660
Maybe if we make the club 
room into a café...

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.910
customers would come pouring 
in, wouldn't they?

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:35.370
Welcome to the DIY Café! Come right in!

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.440
What you need isn't customers, 
it's members, isn't it?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.470
Is it?

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.520
I think turning it into a 
café might be difficult,

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.200
but what about making the club room cuter?

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.700
Cuter?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:52.390
A lot of girls like cute things,

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.890
so that might be a start 
to gaining their interest.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.610
Yeah, I see! You're amazing, Takumin!

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.490
I-I'm not really...

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.070
Come with me after school!

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.080
Of course I will!

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:09.550
I will?

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.470
The DIY club's room is this way.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.070
I see...

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:25.760
What?

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.730
This place isn't for storage? 
It's the DIY club's room?

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:32.950
DIY club

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:36.370
That taxidermy almost looks 
like it's still alive.

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:40.350
Takumin, won't you tell 
the club leader your idea?

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:41.610
The club leader?

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:44.210
Yasaku-san. From year three.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:48.430
What? Do you mean the one who 
chases people around with a hammer?

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:51.260
That's right. That Yasaku-san.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.950
Now, come on in!

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.610
W-Wait!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.390
Come, come!

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:08.230
That storage shed... Is 
it haunted or something?

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.890
Whatcha looking at, Suridecchi?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.660
Suridecchi?

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.330
It's nothing.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:16.910
Really?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:24.260
I wonder if there's something 
in that storage shed, meow?

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.080
Wh-What?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.150
What is that?

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.170
It's a key box.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.960
I thought it'd be better than just a nail.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.640
That finishes it.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:44.070
So.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.480
This is Takumin. She's a classmate!

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.180
Takumin?

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:52.210
U-Um, I...

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:59.260
Takumin came up with a great idea 
for recruiting more club members!

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.880
Come on, Takumin. Tell her.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.290
A-All right.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.500
Um, well...

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.750
Make the club room cuter?

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.440
Y-Yes.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:13.810
Cute, huh?

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:19.410
A novel Takumin likes called 
<i>Snow Cone Girl</i> gave us the idea.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.380
It's <i>Sunflower Girls</i>.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.560
W-Well, then. I'll just go now.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.350
<i>SunGirls</i>, huh?

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:29.390
What?

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.600
Y-Yes. That's right.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.930
And it was turned into a manga, too.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.520
Yes, that <i>SunGirls</i>.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.020
It may not be a bad idea to give it a try.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:44.000
What?

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.900
Do it yourself!

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.770
...self! ...self! ...self!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.220
But right now, the only materials in 
the club room we might be able to use

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.840
to make things cute...

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:04.670
are these tiles.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.720
Hmm...

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.380
If we put them on the walls 
and roof of the club room...

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:13.470
it'll look like a candy 
house out of a fairy tale!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.060
We don't have that many.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.430
Yeah.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:20.800
At most, there might be 
enough to use on a sign.

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:22.800
The sign, huh?

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.990
DIY club

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.940
So, this was the club's sign.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.840
Try it. Do it however you want.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:30.740
Huh?

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.270
However I want?

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:35.850
Isn't that great? She said you can 
do it however you want, Takumin!

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:38.670
After all, it was your idea 
in the first place, right?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.130
No, it wasn't my idea, really.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:45.630
Serufu-san, I only took your 
idea and built on it...

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.840
or sort of grounded it 
in realistic details...

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.940
FOR TILE

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.940
<b>Grout</b>

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.940
<b>White</b>

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.940
Just mix with
 water to use

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:52.940
<b>New Adhesive Mix</b>

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.180
Then, I'll explain.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.740
It's easy.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:52.930
Wh-What?

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:56.390
First, apply adhesive to the 
tile and stick it in place.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:57.560
Easy, right?

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:58.890
Yes, it is.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:03.120
If you use too much adhesive, it'll 
squish out, so use just enough.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.810
If it does squish out, what should we do?

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:09.680
Even if it does, you'll be applying grout 
over the top later, so you can hide it.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.560
It won't be a problem.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.530
But if it's somewhere that can be seen, 
you can cut it away with a knife.

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:17.790
I see.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:21.370
Takumin, you can do it!

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.390
Question, club leader!

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.960
Why do we apply grout?

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:34.260
Grout is something used when 
tiles are placed like this.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:35.620
See?

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.470
There are spaces between the tiles, right?

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.910
Grout is used to fill in those spaces.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:44.370
As the grout dries, it 
fixes the tiles in place.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:46.330
I see.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.830
Something like this?

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.390
Exactly. Even and no gaps.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.280
Nice and neat. Well done.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.540
Thank you!

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.960
You want to make a bench?

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.460
Is that possible?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:00.810
Well...

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.360
We have some old skis. We could use those.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.830
Skis?

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:07.960
Like this.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:10.510
Wow! That's cute!

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:11.660
Right?

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:12.470
Yes!

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.170
Skis are also highly water resistant,

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.510
so they should be fine even 
if they're left outdoors.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.660
Then let's get right to it!

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.520
A bench made of skis, huh?

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.000
I wonder if it'll make Purin happy.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.130
Be careful!

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.080
I'm... fine?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.650
I thought you might not come today.

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:51.450
Congratulations on your 
perfect attendance award.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.490
Thank you very much.

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.200
I was joking.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:14:00.730
<b>Sukonbu 
Snack</b>

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:59.760
Thank you.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:06.920
How is it going? Does it seem 
like you'll find enough members?

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:11.330
Though, you've only had since yesterday. 
Of course you wouldn't have them yet.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.820
Right now, we're working on 
making the club room cuter.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:16.290
Cuter?

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:20.170
Well. Yes, I see.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.000
Club

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.000
You've started with the sign.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.190
Wh-What do you think?

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:29.700
I think it's very good.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.280
It's very carefully done.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.420
The way you used the 
colors is fancy. I like it.

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:37.270
I can't wait to see it when it's done!

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:40.470
Th-Thank you so much!

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.690
But it's already starting to get dark today,

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.150
Club

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.170
so you should wait to keep 
working on it until tomorrow.

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:53.800
It's such a wonderful thing.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:56.960
It makes me remember days gone by.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.670
<b>1 CORNER ONE</b>

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:02.480
Takumin, your bento and your 
notebooks are both neat and pretty.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:04.910
You're really good at detailed work.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.750
Your color sense is impressive too.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:09.450
Not really...

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.290
I think we have some tile at home 
that we aren't able to sell.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:19.730
I'll bring it tomorrow.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:24.350
It'd be nice if Takumin's sign 
brings in lots of new members.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.430
Yeah.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:28.580
Later.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.770
Bye!

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.280
Today was lots of fun.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.670
See you tomorrow!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:37.960
M-Me too!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:39.290
Later!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.910
I-It was...

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.600
fun.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.310
I'm back!

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:47.910
Welcome home!

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.300
A bench made of skis?

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.700
It's not a bench for skiing, though.

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.170
Yes, I understand.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:06.080
Using old skis to make a bench...

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.890
It's an amazing idea, right?

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:14.050
But if we could ski on a bench, 
like you said, that might be fun.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:21.120
I wonder if the bench 
could ride on the lift.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:25.430
They're both seats, so I don't think
 either of them would like it.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.410
Purin! Purin!

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:32.380
My name is Miku!

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:36.060
Which is better, skis or snowboards?

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:36.910
What?

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:41.090
Do you remember there being a bench 
in your backyard when we were little?

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.570
We played there a lot, right?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:47.880
The thing is, in the DIY club, I 
was thinking of building a bench.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.670
Then, just like we did back then...

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:50.440
I don't want it.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:51.450
Huh?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.520
I don't want it!

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:54.430
Purin?

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:58.820
It could be a sled instead...

00:16:58.820 --> 00:16:59.750
Huh?

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.970
Um, club leader?

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.170
This isn't easy for me to say, but...

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.340
I no longer have any need for a bench.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.490
We can put it outside the club room.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.890
It'll be colorful, so it'll 
make a good accent piece.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:20.780
I see.

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:26.220
We can have tea there, and 
eat snacks, and chat...

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:27.350
That sounds good!

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.610
Where's Takumin?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.680
She's already hard at work.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.250
Can I help with something?

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:41.450
Well...

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.790
Take the saw and... No.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.910
Can you use the clamp to secure it?

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:47.670
Got it!

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.530
Is that all right?

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:55.400
Yes.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:57.130
Well done.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.120
And now...

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.950
Perfect attendance.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:50.820
Here.

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.070
The final touch.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:57.820
Got it!

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.450
It's done!

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:05.990
Happy with it?

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.260
Yes!

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:10.590
Wow! You finished it!

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:12.410
Congratulations!

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:14.480
Thanks. How about you?

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.380
Y-Yes.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.840
Club

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:23.040
Wh-What do you think?

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:30.450
It's great.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:35.690
It really is lovely.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:40.850
This might make some students take an 
interest in the DIY club, don't you think?

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:41.690
Yeah!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:45.440
Takumin, thank you! And thanks 
for all your hard work!

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.150
Of course!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.000
Job done, right?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.650
Done...

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.600
<i>So, today was the last day.</i>

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.720
<b>1 CORNER ONE</b>

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:00.160
<i>It was so much fun.</i>

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:03.900
<i>I've never laid tiles before...</i>

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:06.710
<i>but everyone seemed happy...</i>

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:08.850
<i>and they complimented me.</i>

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:12.340
<i>Being invited somewhere by someone...</i>

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:15.210
<i>Being entrusted with something by someone...</i>

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:18.140
<i>Spending time with someone...</i>

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:20.240
<i>I've never done that before.</i>

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.390
<i>For it all to end today...</i>

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.680
<i>I don't want that.</i>

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:29.350
Later.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:30.590
Bye!

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:32.300
U-Um...

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:35.040
Um!

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.620
I'll join the club!

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:43.090
Join the club?

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:45.300
The DIY club?

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:46.290
What?

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:49.240
<i>Huh? Maybe I can't?</i>

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:52.170
You didn't already join?

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:52.950
Huh?

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:55.720
You didn't submit a membership application?

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:56.610
What?

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:00.940
Bring it tomorrow.

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:03.910
I-I will!

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:05.290
Well, then...

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:06.670
See you tomorrow!

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:10.740
Club Leader Yasaku! Serufu-san! 
See you in thirteen hours!

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:18.200
Do it...Yua Serufu.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.760
<b>

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.760
<b>

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.760
<b>

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.970
Club</b></b></b>

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:41.860
Are those... skis?

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:45.810
Which is better, skis or snowboards?

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:48.800
So, what happened to the sled?

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Step 3</b>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Does "DIY" Mean Why Did You Suddenly Show Up?</b>
